          [
            "Explanation",
            "<h3>Vowels and consonants</h3><p>There are <b>5 vowels</b>: A, E, I, O, U (Y is sometimes a vowel). The other 21 letters are <b>consonants</b>.<br><br>English has 26 letters but roughly <b>40 distinct sounds</b>, because letters combine to make new sounds like 'sh', 'ch' and 'th'.</p>"
